WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.367
To escape slavery,

2
00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.200
Ellen Craft posed as

3
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.033
a white male slaveholder.

4
00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:06.267
Her husband William

5
00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:08.333
posed as her enslaved servant.

6
00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:09.367
In 1848,

7
00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:10.733
they traveled openly

8
00:00:10.733 --> 00:00:12.533
by train and steamer.

9
00:00:12.533 --> 00:00:14.033
But Ellen could not write.

10
00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:15.800
What if she had to sign?

11
00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:17.900
She bound her right hand

12
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.300
to make it appear injured—an
excuse not to sign,

13
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.033
reported weeks

14
00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:23.167
after their escape.

15
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.733
Their later book

16
00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:25.700
describes more:

17
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:26.533
bandages hid

18
00:00:26.533 --> 00:00:27.800
her beardless chin,

19
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.467
spectacles obscured her face,

20
00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:30.733
and apparent illness

21
00:00:30.733 --> 00:00:32.667
excused conversation.

22
00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:34.733
William sustained the disguise

23
00:00:34.733 --> 00:00:36.200
as her attendant.

24
00:00:36.333 --> 00:00:38.033
But disguise could not

25
00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:39.333
answer every question.

26
00:00:39.333 --> 00:00:40.333
In Baltimore,

27
00:00:40.333 --> 00:00:41.833
their account says

28
00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:43.333
officials demanded assurance

29
00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:44.767
that the supposed master

30
00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:45.833
had the right

31
00:00:45.833 --> 00:00:47.267
to take William onward.

32
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:48.700
Appearance was not

33
00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:49.967
proof of ownership.

34
00:00:50.233 --> 00:00:51.533
William’s account says

35
00:00:51.533 --> 00:00:52.867
a conductor confirmed

36
00:00:52.867 --> 00:00:54.600
their earlier train journey.

37
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.000
As departure approached,

38
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.333
the officer let them through,

39
00:00:58.333 --> 00:00:59.700
citing the apparent

40
00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:00.633
master’s illness.

41
00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:02.167
After four days,

42
00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:03.567
they reached Philadelphia.

43
00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:04.867
Reaching the North

44
00:01:04.867 --> 00:01:06.600
did not guarantee safety.

45
00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:07.433
In 1850,

46
00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:09.067
men came to Boston

47
00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:10.300
to recapture them.

48
00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.400
The Crafts left for England.

49
00:01:12.633 --> 00:01:13.567
Their ingenuity

50
00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:15.400
turned a system’s assumptions

51
00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:16.300
against it.

52
00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.333
Treated as property,

53
00:01:17.333 --> 00:01:18.367
they escaped together

54
00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:19.733
by making it appear

55
00:01:19.733 --> 00:01:21.433
that one owned the other.
